  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact Cluster: Tech Academy in Nigeria and Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Nigeria and Uganda, there is an abundant supply of ICT graduates. In both countries, there is a certain capacity for formal ICT education (both public and private). However, learning offerings regarding international coding standards and professional skills are limited, and the offerings regarding the ability to promote oneself and to build up experience (e.g. through internships/traineeships) lack completely.The project&apos;s purpose is to create crucial new training capacity for software developers in Uganda and Nigeria that will enable them to become a professional software developers for the international market. Important components of the training capacity are:&#x2022;	Self-paced learning;&#x2022;	Peer-reviewed training;&#x2022;	Project-based learning;&#x2022;	Guided internships/jobs;&#x2022;	Guided career development;&#x2022;	Specialisation tracks.All are aimed at creating software developers that are able to compete at an international level. In this way, the project will contribute to an improved ICT structure, improved economic opportunities and improved access to markets.</narrative>
  </description>
